<title>USA: Netherlands top origin for perishables at JFK in'96.</title>
<headline>Netherlands top origin for perishables at JFK in'96.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States Department of Agriculture at John F. Kennedy Airport said the Netherlands was the top airport gateway for perishable imports into the airport during 1996.</p>
<p>The top ten originating gateways of perishable imports were:</p>
<p>1.  Netherlands</p>
<p>2.  Israel</p>
<p>3.  Dominican Republic</p>
<p>4.  Jamaica</p>
<p>5.  Italy</p>
<p>6.  France</p>
<p>7.  Belgium</p>
<p>8.  Colombia</p>
<p>9.  Chile</p>
<p>10. South Africa</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017</p>
